.TH MPC 1 "2025-01-03" "MPC v1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mpc \- translate Unix man pages into working CLI utilities via LLMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpc
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I INPUT.1
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mpc
utility is a documentation-driven compiler that translates Unix man page
documentation (.1 files) into actual working command-line utilities using
Large Language Models.
.PP
Rather than writing code to match documentation,
.B mpc
reads your man page and generates the actual working binary that implements
exactly what the documentation describes. This represents a paradigm shift
where documentation becomes executable specification.
.PP
.B mpc
parses the input man page, generates a structured specification for an LLM,
calls the LLM API to generate C code, and compiles the result into a
native executable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Specify output executable name. Default is the input filename without
the .1 extension.
.TP
.BR \-m " " \fIMODEL\fR
Specify LLM model to use. Default is \fIcodellama:7b\fR for local Ollama,
or \fIgemini-1.5-flash\fR when using --remote.
.TP
.BR \-u " " \fIURL\fR
Specify Ollama server URL. Default is \fIhttp://localhost:11434\fR.
.TP
.BR \-r " " \fIRETRIES\fR
Maximum number of retry attempts with error feedback. When compilation fails,
.B mpc
will capture compiler errors and send them back to the LLM for improved
code generation. Default is 3 attempts.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output showing generated specifications, LLM responses,
and detailed compilation feedback.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug mode. Keeps intermediate files and shows extracted code
for inspection.
.TP
.BR \-\-remote
Use remote Gemini API instead of local Ollama. Requires GEMINI_API_KEY
environment variable to be set.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GEMINI_API_KEY
Required when using the --remote flag. Contains the API key for
Google's Gemini API. Get one from https://aistudio.google.com/
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./bin/mpc
Default location of the mpc binary when built from source.
.TP
.I build/*.c
Generated C source files (kept when using -d flag).
.TP
.I examples/*.1
Example man pages included with the distribution.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile a simple man page:
.nf
.RS
$ mpc examples/hello.1
📖 Parsing man page...
✓ Parsed man page: hello (6 sections, 3 options, 0 examples)
📝 Generating structured specification... (attempt 1/3)
🤖 Generating code via codellama:7b...
✓ Generated 947 bytes of code
🔍 Extracting code from LLM response...
🔧 Compiling to executable... (attempt 1/3)
🔧 Compiling C code to executable...
✅ Compilation successful on attempt 1

✅ Success! Generated executable: examples/hello
📊 File size: 33704 bytes
$ ./examples/hello
Hello, World!
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compile with custom output name and verbose logging:
.nf
.RS
$ mpc -o calculator -v examples/calculator.1
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use a different local model:
.nf
.RS
$ mpc -m deepseek-coder examples/count.1
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use remote Gemini API with increased retries:
.nf
.RS
$ export GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
$ mpc --remote -r 5 -m gemini-1.5-pro examples/calculator.1
.RE
.fi
.PP
Debug a failed compilation:
.nf
.RS
$ mpc -d -v examples/complex.1
# Examine generated code if compilation fails
$ cat build/complex.c
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B mpc
exits with one of the following values:
.TP
.B 0
Success. The man page was compiled successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Error. Compilation failed after all retry attempts, invalid arguments,
or missing dependencies.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B mpc
may produce the following messages:
.TP
.B "Error: Cannot open file INPUT.1: No such file or directory"
The specified input file does not exist or is not readable.
.TP
.B "Error: GEMINI_API_KEY environment variable not set"
The --remote flag was used but no API key was provided.
.TP
.B "Error: LLM request failed: Connection refused"
Cannot connect to the Ollama server. Make sure it's running with 'ollama serve'.
.TP
.B "❌ Compilation failed on attempt N/M"
The generated C code failed to compile. Error details are captured and
sent as feedback for the next retry attempt.
.TP
.B "💥 Max retries exceeded. Final compilation failed."
All retry attempts were exhausted and compilation still failed.
.SH NOTES
.B mpc
generates C code exclusively because LLMs have been extensively trained on
Linux kernel source code and POSIX documentation, making them exceptionally
good at generating clean, portable C code.
.PP
The intelligent retry system captures compilation errors and feeds them back
to the LLM, dramatically improving success rates from ~75% to ~90%+ for
complex man pages.
.PP
Generated binaries are native executables with no runtime dependencies and
typically range from 30KB to 100KB in size.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B mpc
requires the following to build and run:
.IP \(bu 4
C compiler (clang preferred on macOS, gcc on Linux)
.IP \(bu 4
libcurl development headers
.IP \(bu 4
jansson JSON library
.IP \(bu 4
Either Ollama (local) or Gemini API key (remote)
.SH BUGS
Complex man pages with intricate logic may require multiple retry attempts.
The quality of generated code depends on the clarity and completeness of
the input man page specification.
.PP
Report bugs to: https://github.com/yourusername/man-page-compiler/issues
